From 3dcd2b329dc0c3c36dc18f905b78d154364ba180 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aryan Randeriya <aryan.k.randeriya@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 16:33:32 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 03/18] fix(modules): load data: and blob: module scripts
 locally

Module scripts from data: URLs were sent to the network layer, which only
fetches http(s)/file, and blob: URLs from URL.createObjectURL lived only in a
JS-side map the Rust module loader could not see. Bing's blob: module scripts
and Reddit's inline data: modules therefore failed to load.

The module loader now decodes data: URLs with the shared decoder (moved from
obscura-browser into obscura-net) and reads blob: URLs from a page-scoped
object-URL store that createObjectURL/revokeObjectURL maintain through ops.
A blob: module resolves only if this page minted it, for the document's
origin, and has not revoked it; the store is cleared with each new document.
Workers read the same store, replacing the enumerable __blobStore global.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tm2SNEJ42hMPiZ6cFb8Vih
